1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,087
The Rise of GLP-1 Drugs: A New Era in Weight Management.

2
00:00:05,037 --> 00:00:14,325
GLP-1 receptor agonists, originally developed for type 2 diabetes, have emerged as a transformative class of medications for weight management.

3
00:00:14,325 --> 00:00:25,375
These drugs mimic glucagon-like peptide-1, an incretin hormone that stimulates insulin secretion, slows gastric emptying, and acts on hypothalamic receptors to reduce appetite.

4
00:00:25,375 --> 00:00:42,912
Semaglutide (marketed as Wegovy for obesity), a once-weekly injectable GLP-1 analogue developed by Novo Nordisk, demonstrated a mean weight reduction of approximately 15 percent in the STEP 1 clinical trial published in The New England Journal of Medicine (Wilding et al., 2021).

5
00:00:42,912 --> 00:00:59,187
Tirzepatide (Mounjaro/Zepbound), a dual GIP and GLP-1 receptor agonist developed by Eli Lilly, achieved even greater reductions of up to 22.5 percent in the SURMOUNT-1 trial (Jastreboff et al., NEJM, 2022).

6
00:00:59,187 --> 00:01:02,750
The mechanism extends beyond appetite suppression.

7
00:01:02,750 --> 00:01:21,650
GLP-1 drugs improve glycemic control, reduce cardiovascular events -- the SELECT trial (NEJM, 2024) found semaglutide reduced major adverse cardiovascular events by 20 percent in patients with overweight or obesity -- and show promise in reducing inflammation through effects on immune cells.

8
00:01:21,650 --> 00:01:34,812
Phase 2 trials of oral non-peptide GLP-1 agonists reported in Nature Medicine (2024) suggest that oral alternatives may become available, potentially improving accessibility for broader populations.

9
00:01:34,812 --> 00:01:41,000
Side effects include nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea, which typically diminish over time.

10
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:46,362
Concerns about pancreatic safety and gastroparesis remain under investigation.

11
00:01:46,362 --> 00:01:53,225
The global demand has led to periodic shortages, prompting regulatory scrutiny of compounding pharmacies.

12
00:01:53,225 --> 00:02:05,825
GLP-1 drugs represent a paradigm shift in obesity treatment, moving beyond lifestyle modification alone toward pharmacotherapy that targets the underlying neuroendocrine biology of appetite regulation.

